    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-blue);\" data-correct=\"B,D,E\" data-multi=\"1\" data-rationale=\"Amazon API Gateway allows you to create, publish, maintain, monitor, and secure APIs at any scale. It enables customers to make HTTP API calls to interact with your application.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;As a developer you are tasked with creating an application so that your customers can leverage your microservices by making HTTP API calls. Your goal is to create an event-driven architecture to support this application. What combination of AWS Services can you use so that your customers can make the HTTP API calls, serverless compute containing the business logic processes the incoming API calls, and the corresponding microservices data can be persistently stored? (SELECT THREE)&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Amazon CloudWatch&quot;, &quot;Amazon API Gateway&quot;, &quot;AWS Secrets Manager&quot;, &quot;Amazon DynamoDB&quot;, &quot;AWS Lambda&quot;, &quot;AWS Elastic Beanstalk&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Amazon API Gateway; Amazon DynamoDB; AWS Lambda&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Amazon API Gateway allows you to create, publish, maintain, monitor, and secure APIs at any scale. It enables customers to make HTTP API calls to interact with your application.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;While Amazon CloudWatch is a monitoring service for AWS resources and applications, it is not directly related to creating an event-driven architecture for handling HTTP API calls and persistently storing microservices data.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;Amazon API Gateway allows you to create, publish, maintain, monitor, and secure APIs at any scale. It enables customers to make HTTP API calls to interact with your application.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;AWS Secrets Manager is a service that helps you protect access to your applications, services, and IT resources. While it plays a crucial role in managing secrets, it is not directly involved in creating an event-driven architecture for handling HTTP API calls and persistently storing microservices data.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;Amazon DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database service that provides fast and predictable performance with seamless scalability. It can persistently store the microservices data.&quot;, &quot;E&quot;: &quot;AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service that runs your code in response to events and automatically scales to handle them. It can contain the business logic processes for handling the incoming API calls without provisioning or managing servers.&quot;, &quot;F&quot;: &quot;AWS Elastic Beanstalk is an easy-to-use service for deploying and scaling web applications and services. However, it is not specifically designed for creating event-driven architectures or handling HTTP API calls and persistently storing microservices data in a serverless manner.&quot;}}\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 1 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 1 of 6</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">select all that apply</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">As a developer you are tasked with creating an application so that your customers can leverage your microservices by making HTTP API calls. Your goal is to create an event-driven architecture to support this application. What combination of AWS Services can you use so that your customers can make the HTTP API calls, serverless compute containing the business logic processes the incoming API calls, and the corresponding microservices data can be persistently stored? (SELECT THREE)</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Amazon CloudWatch</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Amazon API Gateway</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">AWS Secrets Manager</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Amazon DynamoDB</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"E\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">E</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">AWS Lambda</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"F\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">F</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">AWS Elastic Beanstalk</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-submit\"><button class=\"sm-submit\" type=\"button\" disabled>Submit</button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Exam Strategy Session 1 Answer Key</div></div>",
